To rigorously verify mathematical correctness, the textbook example 'Ends with ab' is manually solved step-by-step.

• Problem Statement:
Construct an equivalent DFA for the NFA accepting all strings over Σ = {a, b} that end in the substring 'ab'.

• NFA Specification:
Q = {q0, q1, q2},  Σ = {a, b},  Start = q0,  Accepting F = {q2}
Transition Function δ:
   - δ(q0, a) = {q0, q1}
   - δ(q0, b) = {q0}
   - δ(q1, b) = {q2}
   - δ(q1, a) = ∅,  δ(q2, a) = ∅,  δ(q2, b) = ∅

